+2.1 By stationarity [F1] and the chain rule [F3], $$H_n=\sum_{k=0}^{n-1}H(X_k\mid X_0^{k-1})=\sum_{k=0}^{n-1}H(X_0\mid X_{-k}^{-1})=\sum_{k=0}^{n-1}\int g_k\,dP.$$ Cesàro convergence and step 1.5 give $\lim_nH_n/n=\int g_\infty\,dP$; [F4] identifies this limit as $h$. This also covers zero-probability transitions, which are never observed. [F1, F2, F3, F4, step 1.5, algebra] ∎
